@startuml
' =============================================================================
' Agentic retrieval — AgenticRetrieveStream in each maxAgentIteration mode — UML sequence diagram
'
' Mermaid source set : diagrams/mermaid/09-agentic-retrieval.md (view C)
' Chapter            : 01-amazon-bedrock/agentic-retrieval/01-agentic-retrieval.md
' Verified           : 2026-11-15
' Status             : academy design, not an official AWS reference architecture.
'                      AWS documents the steps and the events, not the implementation.
'                      No AWS icons; nothing is included from the network.
'
' Official sources this view relies on:
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/kb-test-agentic-retrieve.html
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/APIReference/API_agent-runtime_AgenticRetrieveStream.html
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/APIReference/API_agent-runtime_AgenticRetrieveConfiguration.html
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/kb-test-agentic-retrieve-instruction.html
'   https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/single-shot-and-agentic-retrieval-with-amazon-bedrock-managed-knowledge-base/
'   https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/agentic-retrieval-for-amazon-bedrock-managed-knowledge-base/
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/kb-managed-observability.html
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/kb-managed-quotas.html
'
' What UML adds over the Mermaid view: trust boundaries as boxes, and the three
' modes as one alt fragment so the cost of each mode can be read as message count.
' =============================================================================
!pragma layout smetana
title AgenticRetrieveStream — one request in each maxAgentIteration mode (UML sequence)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #888888
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor #666666
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam noteBorderColor #888888
skinparam legendBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam legendBorderColor #888888

autonumber
box "Your AWS account 111122223333 · one Region with managed knowledge bases" #FFFBF5
  participant "Your application\nIAM role: AgenticRetrieveStream · Retrieve\nGetDocumentContent · InvokeModelWithResponseStream" as App #FDEBD0
  database "Amazon Bedrock AgentCore Memory\noptional · same account" as MEM #EDE7F6
end box
box "AWS-managed boundary · Amazon Bedrock" #F5FBF6
  participant "Amazon Bedrock runtime API\nbedrock-agent-runtime\nquota 300 requests per minute per account" as RT #E6F4EA
  participant "Planner and answer model\nMANAGED · or your CUSTOM model,\ninvoked with your credentials and quotas" as FM #E6F4EA
  database "Managed knowledge bases\n1 to 5 retrievers" as KB #EDE7F6
end box

App -> RT : AgenticRetrieveStream (messages, retrievers, agenticRetrieveConfiguration)
note over App, RT : TLS and SigV4 · the caller's role needs every permission the run uses
RT -> RT : Validate instruction, guardrail type, memory fields and mode
opt memoryConfiguration with sessionBinding
  RT -> MEM : ListEvents for actorId and sessionId
  MEM --> RT : USER and ASSISTANT events
  RT --> App : traceEvent (session history load)
end

alt maxAgentIteration 0 with generateResponse false
  RT -> KB : One retrieval
  KB --> RT : Passages
  RT --> App : result with passages only (no score, no location)
else maxAgentIteration 1 — single-shot RAG
  RT -> KB : One retrieval
  KB --> RT : Passages
  RT -> FM : Generate the answer from the passages
  FM --> RT : Answer and citations
  RT --> App : responseEvent chunks, then result
else maxAgentIteration 2 to 5 — agentic
  RT -> KB : Speculative retrieval (raw query or routing probe)
  KB --> RT : Candidate passages
  RT --> App : traceEvent SpeculativeRetrieval
  loop Up to n minus 1 planning rounds; stops early when evidence is sufficient
    RT -> FM : Plan sub-queries and judge sufficiency
    FM --> RT : retrieve actions, or a memoryRetrieve action
    RT --> App : traceEvent Planning
    RT -> KB : Retrieve for each sub-query
    KB --> RT : Passages
    opt Planner chose memoryRetrieve
      RT -> MEM : RetrieveMemoryRecords in the configured namespace
      MEM --> RT : Memory records
    end
    opt A passage is not enough context
      RT -> KB : GetDocumentContent
      KB --> RT : Full document
    end
    RT --> App : traceEvent Retrieval or FullDocumentExpansion
  end
  RT -> FM : Generate the answer from all collected results
  FM --> RT : Answer and citations
  RT --> App : responseEvent chunks
  RT --> App : result with deduplicated results, answer and citations
end

note over RT, FM : With policyConfiguration (CUSTOM model type only) the guardrail\nis applied during the run and can only BLOCK
opt sessionBinding with persistenceMode DEFAULT
  RT -> MEM : CreateEvent with the question and the generated answer
end

note across
  One iteration is one foundation model call; the last iteration is reserved for writing the answer,
  so maxAgentIteration n allows up to n − 1 planning rounds. The speculative retrieval does not count as an iteration.
  Exceptions arrive as events in the stream: validationException and serviceQuotaExceededException (400), accessDeniedException (403),
  resourceNotFoundException (404), conflictException (409), dependencyFailedException (424), throttlingException (429),
  internalServerException (500), badGatewayException (502).
end note

legend right
  |= Notation |= Meaning |
  | solid arrow | request or call |
  | dashed arrow | response, or an event on the open stream |
  | alt / loop / opt | mode, planning rounds, optional step |
  |<#FDEBD0> orange | your compute |
  |<#E6F4EA> green | Amazon Bedrock |
  |<#EDE7F6> purple | data at rest |
  Academy design · not an official AWS diagram · Verified 2026-11-15
endlegend
@enduml
